      "title": "Divergent Integration Models: Runtime vs. API Layer",
      "summary": "The ecosystem split hinges on architectural lock-in. Letta functions as a full agent runtime where agents execute within an OS-inspired multi-tiered memory environment (Core/RAM, Recall/Cache, Archival/Cold). Conversely, Mem0 acts as a decoupled API layer easily bolted onto diverse orchestration frameworks (like LangChain or AWS Agent SDK) and focuses on hierarchical state isolation across user, persona, and session boundaries.",
